rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":69.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.0721960238446751,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.019471667490830624,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":47.8,"_gate_rev_durability":0.12157955411744292,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":85.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03365833519142206,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":48.5,"_gate_share_shrink":0.09026526015648795,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00890979608686567,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.0212,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":14.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"WesBanco, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for WesBanco Bank, Inc. that provides retail banking, corporate banking, personal and corporate trust, brokerage, mortgage banking, and insurance services to individuals and businesses in the United States. It operates in two segments, Community Banking, and Trust and Investment Services. The company accepts interest and non-interest-bearing demand, money market, and savings deposit accounts, as well as certificates of deposit; and offers land and construction, improved property, commercial and industrial, residential real estate mortgage, and consumer loans, as well as home equity lines of credit and overdrafts. It also provides mutual funds and annuities; and property, casualty, life, and title insurance services, as well as holds commercial real estate properties and investment securities. In addition, the company offers letters of credit and international wire services, as well as operates as an investment adviser to a family of mutual funds. It operates through branches and ATM machines in West Virginia, Ohio, western Pennsylvania, Kentucky, southern Indiana, Michigan, and Maryland. WesBanco, Inc. was founded in 1870 and is headquartered in Wheeling, West Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey H. Jackson | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $327K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $93K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["WesBanco, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.7B market cap on $981M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $280M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.30\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 37% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"WesBanco, Inc. $WSB